  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Use the division algorithm to divide $P(x)$ by $D(x)$. Express each result in the form $P(x)=D(x)Q(x)+R(x)$, where either $R(x)=0$ or the degree of $R(x)$ is less than the degree of $D(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^2+6x+1$, $D(x)=x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2+6x+1=(x+2)(x+4)-7$.",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms, multiply by the divisor, and subtract at each stage:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^2\\div x&=x\\\\(x^2+6x+1)-x(x+2)&=4x+1\\\\4x\\div x&=4\\\\(4x+1)-4(x+2)&=-7.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x+4$ and $R(x)=-7$, so\n$$x^2+6x+1=(x+2)(x+4)-7.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3-5x^2-12x+30$, $D(x)=x+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3-5x^2-12x+30=(x+5)(x^2-10x+38)-160$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x^3\\div x&=x^2\\\\(x^3-5x^2-12x+30)-x^2(x+5)&=-10x^2-12x+30\\\\-10x^2\\div x&=-10x\\\\(-10x^2-12x+30)-(-10x)(x+5)&=38x+30\\\\38x\\div x&=38\\\\(38x+30)-38(x+5)&=-160.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x^2-10x+38$ and $R(x)=-160$, so\n$$x^3-5x^2-12x+30=(x+5)(x^2-10x+38)-160.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=5x^3-7x^2-6$, $D(x)=x-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5x^3-7x^2-6=(x-3)(5x^2+8x+24)+66$.",
          "worked": "Include $0x$ for the missing power.\n$$\\begin{aligned}5x^3\\div x&=5x^2\\\\(5x^3-7x^2+0x-6)-5x^2(x-3)&=8x^2+0x-6\\\\8x^2\\div x&=8x\\\\(8x^2+0x-6)-8x(x-3)&=24x-6\\\\24x\\div x&=24\\\\(24x-6)-24(x-3)&=66.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $Q(x)=5x^2+8x+24$ and $R(x)=66$, so\n$$5x^3-7x^2-6=(x-3)(5x^2+8x+24)+66.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^4+3x^2-3x$, $D(x)=x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^4+3x^2-3x=(x+2)(x^3-2x^2+7x-17)+34$.",
          "worked": "Include zero coefficients for the missing powers.\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^4\\div x&=x^3\\\\(x^4+0x^3+3x^2-3x+0)-x^3(x+2)&=-2x^3+3x^2-3x\\\\-2x^3\\div x&=-2x^2\\\\(-2x^3+3x^2-3x)-(-2x^2)(x+2)&=7x^2-3x\\\\7x^2\\div x&=7x\\\\(7x^2-3x)-7x(x+2)&=-17x\\\\-17x\\div x&=-17\\\\-17x-(-17)(x+2)&=34.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x^3-2x^2+7x-17$ and $R(x)=34$, so\n$$x^4+3x^2-3x=(x+2)(x^3-2x^2+7x-17)+34.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=4x^3-4x^2+1$, $D(x)=2x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4x^3-4x^2+1=(2x+1)\\left(2x^2-3x+\\frac32\\right)-\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "Include $0x$ for the missing power.\n$$\\begin{aligned}4x^3\\div(2x)&=2x^2\\\\(4x^3-4x^2+0x+1)-2x^2(2x+1)&=-6x^2+0x+1\\\\-6x^2\\div(2x)&=-3x\\\\(-6x^2+0x+1)-(-3x)(2x+1)&=3x+1\\\\3x\\div(2x)&=\\frac32\\\\(3x+1)-\\frac32(2x+1)&=-\\frac12.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $Q(x)=2x^2-3x+\\frac32$ and $R(x)=-\\frac12$, so\n$$4x^3-4x^2+1=(2x+1)\\left(2x^2-3x+\\frac32\\right)-\\frac12.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^4+3x^3-3x^2-4x+1$, $D(x)=x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^4+3x^3-3x^2-4x+1=(x+1)(x^3+2x^2-5x+1)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x^4\\div x&=x^3\\\\(x^4+3x^3-3x^2-4x+1)-x^3(x+1)&=2x^3-3x^2-4x+1\\\\2x^3\\div x&=2x^2\\\\(2x^3-3x^2-4x+1)-2x^2(x+1)&=-5x^2-4x+1\\\\-5x^2\\div x&=-5x\\\\(-5x^2-4x+1)-(-5x)(x+1)&=x+1\\\\x\\div x&=1\\\\(x+1)-1(x+1)&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x^3+2x^2-5x+1$ and $R(x)=0$, so\n$$x^4+3x^3-3x^2-4x+1=(x+1)(x^3+2x^2-5x+1).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
